Revert upstream 0d743a71 ("globalshortcuts: Do not register shortcuts on
session creation", FIXED-IN 6.7.4).

Chromium/Electron (GlobalAcceleratorListenerLinux::OnListShortcuts) skips
BindShortcuts when every shortcut id is already returned by ListShortcuts.
Since 6.7.4 stored shortcuts are listed but no longer registered with
kglobalaccel until BindShortcuts, so they stay inactive from the second
launch on (e.g. Claude Desktop quick entry hotkey).

--- a/src/globalshortcuts.cpp
+++ b/src/globalshortcuts.cpp
@@ -479,6 +479,8 @@ void GlobalShortcutsSession::loadActions()
         action->setObjectName(name);
         action->setText(info.friendlyName());
         action->setShortcuts(info.keys());
+        // Explicitly load existing global shortcut setting
+        KGlobalAccel::self()->setShortcut(action.get(), action->shortcuts(), KGlobalAccel::Autoloading);
     }
 }
 
